# Settings

**Settings → Storage** (`settings/storage.tsx`): the daemon's groups (`GET /v1/storage`) plus main's share (`getAppStorage` over the daemon's `unclaimed` names). A clean-up is the daemon's background job: the page posts it on the confirming press and, while it runs, polls `GET /v1/storage/job` (never the measuring `GET /v1/storage`) one request at a time, `STORAGE_JOB_POLL_MS` after each answer, then measures once. Compact is the exception: the daemon only schedules it, and the page then restarts the daemon (`restartDaemon`), which compacts before it serves anything; the outcome is read from the restarted daemon's `job`. The In use card leads with the total and `SegmentBar`; its per-group breakdown and folder path open from Breakdown. The rest are `settings/storage-row.tsx` rows in named groups (Chats, Tasks, Teams and app, the last largest first): dot in the part's bar colour, name, actions, figure in one right-aligned column, and what it is and holds behind a press on the line, folded on every visit. The five largest parts of at least 1% get a colour; the others share one neutral stretch of the bar. Only what destroys something is red. Archived chats are deleted by age (`ArchivedChatsRow`): older than the picked period, or all. Each of `chats.archivedPeriods` carries the daemon's count and the cutoff it counted, posted back verbatim as `archivedBefore`, so the page never computes a date and deletes what it showed. Hidden on a paired phone.

**Lessons (`chats/lessons-*.ts*`, `components/lessons-card.tsx`):** Reflect now is a row-menu item (`chat-list-item.tsx` `onReflect`) and the agents panel's lightbulb (`ReflectNowButton`, its state from `useThreadLessons`, `GET /v1/chats/:runId/lessons`, re-read every 5 s while a reflection works); neither is offered on an analysis chat or a paired device. The card is drawn from the `lessons` row a reflection writes into the thread, with each lesson's newest `lesson_outcome` row folded on (`lessons-payload.ts`, the twin of the daemon's `LessonsPayloadSchema`; an old row reads `check: null` and `by: 'user'`): a lesson filed on its own reads "Saved to memory · <scope> · Searchable only" with Undo and Edit, one waiting for review offers Approve, an undone or already-remembered one collapses, lessons the check dropped fold under one line with their reasons, and a lesson with no outcome reads as one meta line (source thread, signal, refines / broken-again), its title and rule, a Why fold (reason and evidence), and one primary `SplitButton` naming its outcome ("Save to <target>", "Update <handle>" for a `refines` memory lesson, "Move up to the memory index" for a `broken_again` one — the twin of the daemon's `moveUpOf`; the project's instructions stay a target in its menu), whose menu picks what the button does: the targets (memory and its scopes, the project's instructions, a member's instructions from the payload's `places.members`, a new or existing project knowledge document read through `KnowledgeApi` only when the menu opens; a target the thread has no place for is listed disabled), and for an update or a move up, saving as a new entry instead; Edit and Reject stay ghost buttons beside it, and a lesson saved outside memory names its place and offers no Undo or Edit. Settings → Memory's Waiting for review tab holds an Entries | Lessons switch, and the tab's count adds the lessons to the waiting entries; Lessons (`settings/waiting-lessons.tsx`) is `GET /v1/lessons/proposals?status=proposed,check_failed` — every lesson waiting on the user, a deleted thread's included — drawn with the card's own lesson row, then Saved to memory (`SavedLessons`, `?status=saved` kept to `undoable`, newest five with Show all) with the card's own decided row, Undo and Edit. The Settings nav-rail count and the Memory row inside Settings add those waiting lessons to the waiting entries (`settings/use-memory-waiting-count.ts`, re-read on memory and lessons changes and a reconnect), the same number as the tab. `LessonsApiContext` and `LessonsJumpContext` (provided by `ChatProviders`) give it those actions and Show in thread; its footer reads `GET /v1/lessons/reflections/:id` for the reflection and, when the row names one, the check — "cost not reported" where the CLI reports none. After an archive `Chats` watches `lessons_changed` for that thread for up to 10 s and shows `components/action-notice.tsx` (compact: title, model and price, one Skip, 8 s, paused on hover) only when `GET /v1/lessons/segments?status=queued` returns a stretch; Skip is `POST .../skip`, and a 409 (already started) closes it quietly. The delete dialog asks `GET /v1/lessons/estimate` and shows Extract lessons first, unchecked on every open, only when `signals > 0`. Price and title text go through `chats/lesson-labels.ts`, so a sub-cent price reads `<$0.01` everywhere. Settings → Memory → Lessons (`settings/lessons-settings.tsx`) picks the one Memory model (default Same as the thread: the thread's own CLI, profile, model and effort) and the checker, says from Memory's Agent notes (passed in as `agentWrites`) whether a memory lesson is saved at once or waits for review, with the composer's own `TargetSelect` plus `ChoiceModelSettings` (`settings/memory-triage-settings.tsx`, the model settings menu with its profile, model, effort, window and parameters) and reads `GET /v1/lessons/spend`. Stats shows reflection and check spend in one line under the breakdowns (`stats/lessons-spend-line.tsx`, the daemon's `byPurpose`). A project's page (`projects/project-lessons-card.tsx`) and a team's Memory tab carry `LessonsOverrideControl` (inherit / on / off), locked while the app's mode is Off (`useAppLessonsMode`).

**Knowledge (`knowledge/`, `#/knowledge[/<id>]`):** the list over every place (`Knowledge.tsx`, `knowledge-row.tsx`), one document (`knowledge-document-view.tsx`) with its history (`knowledge-history.tsx`), the form (`knowledge-form.tsx`, `MdEditor` opened on `preview='edit'` with `highlight={false}`, since a live preview or syntax colouring redoes 256 KB on every key), and the review of what agents propose (`knowledge-review.tsx`, drawn with `UnifiedDiff` over the daemon's `diff`). Lists are the daemon's and body-free, re-read on `knowledge_changed` (`daemon-client.ts` `onKnowledgeChanged`). A `409 KNOWLEDGE_STALE` keeps the typed text and offers Reload; a stale proposal offers its text, never Approve. An unreviewed `active` document and any whole text under review are drawn raw (`knowledge-raw-text.tsx`), because rendered Markdown drops comments and unused link references. The transcript's tool row re-reads its documents in the run's own places when it opens (`KnowledgeLoaderContext`, `listKnowledge({handle, runId})`), or in the place its call named with `project` or `team` (`headsInNamedPlace`), so it shows what they are now; a search whose result came back with no text, as cursor-agent reports a successful MCP result, asks `GET /v1/knowledge/runs/:runId/search`, the same search the agent's tool runs. The rail's count and the project page's section read `GET /v1/knowledge/counts`. Markdown export goes through `saveKnowledgeExport`, refused on a paired device.

